## **Why Choose Private Pistol Lessons at the NRA Range in Fairfax, VA?**

One-on-One Private Instruction at Live Fire Instruction provides direct, personalized coaching tailored specifically to your individual skill level, goals, and comfort. Operating out of the world-class **NRA Headquarters Range** at **11250 Waples Mill Rd in Fairfax, VA**, our 60-minute private shooting lessons deliver concentrated, distraction-free training that accelerates your learning curve far beyond group classroom settings.

Whether you are seeking **private shooting lessons in Northern Virginia** to safely handle a handgun for the first time or looking for an experienced **NRA Range private instructor** to refine defensive marksmanship, our certified team adapts each session to match your personal pace.

---

## **Who Is Private Firearm Instruction For?**

* **First-Time & Beginner Shooters:** Experience a calm, non-intimidating environment to learn basic firearm safety, handgun operation, and fundamental shooting mechanics under continuous 1-on-1 supervision.
* **Concealed Carry (CCW) Permit Holders:** Refine your draw stroke, sight acquisition, and recoil management for real-world defensive readiness.
* **Handgun Owners Testing New Equipment:** Get expert guidance on zeroing sights, adjusting grip, and mastering your specific firearm model (glocks, revolvers, semi-autos).
* **Shooters Overcoming Bad Habits or Shot Deviation:** Target specific shooting tendencies—such as anticipating recoil or slapping the trigger—with immediate real-time feedback.

---

## **Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)**

#### **Do I need my own firearm for private lessons?**
**No.** You do not need to own a firearm to take private shooting lessons with Live Fire Instruction. We provide handguns for use during your session. If you already own a personal firearm that you plan to carry or use for home defense, we strongly encourage bringing it so our instructors can help you master your specific equipment.

#### **Can absolute beginners take 1-on-1 shooting classes?**
**Yes, absolutely.** In fact, 1-on-1 private lessons are often the single best starting point for total beginners. You receive the full, undivided attention of an NRA-certified instructor who guides you through safety protocol, loading, aiming, and firing at a pace that feels completely comfortable and safe for you.

#### **What range fees or ammunition costs should I expect at the NRA Range?**
Lesson tuition ($75.00/hr for one student, $125.00/hr total for two students) covers your professional instruction. Range lane fees and ammunition costs are separate and paid directly to the NRA Range upon arrival. Ammunition and range accessories can also be purchased on-site at the NRA Range pro shop.

